      "side": 1,
      "message": "from https://git-scm.com/docs/api-trace2#_enabling_a_target: \"`\u003cabsolute-pathname\u003e` - ... If the target already exists and is a directory, the traces will be written to files (one per process) underneath the given directory.\"\n\nas-is, if target is a dir, open will raise a `IsADirectoryError` and silently swallowed by the `except OSError`\n\nrepo solved this by checking isdir, then making a NamedTemporaryFile under it: https://cs.opensource.google/gerrit/gerrit/git-repo/+/main:git_trace2_event_log_base.py;l\u003d350-367;drc\u003da27dbcdb7bba1b8a2cc84112fa31c8f9f818604e",
